### Feature Users — UPDATE (PUT / PATCH) y CAMBIO DE CONTRASEÑA
### Ni PUT ni PATCH cambian `password` ni `status`.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
@id = 2

### LOGIN como admin (ejecutar PRIMERO: guarda el token en @token)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### PUT — reemplazo completo
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "caja",
  "email": "caja@tazanorte.local",
  "avatar": "https://tazanorte.local/avatars/caja.png"
}

### PATCH — parcial. `password` y `status` se ignoran (no son del DTO)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios/{{id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "avatar": null,
  "password": "hackeada",
  "status": "inactive"
}

### CAMBIO DE CONTRASEÑA — exige la contraseña ACTUAL
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios/{{id}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "Caja123!",
  "new_password": "Caja456!"
}

### Devolver la contraseña original (ISS-22 hace login con Caja123!)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios/{{id}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "Caja456!",
  "new_password": "Caja123!"
}

### 400 — contraseña actual incorrecta
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios/{{id}}/password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "otra",
  "new_password": "Caja789!"
}
